# Free Guild, coins, sinks and merit-lite (design/data/economy.toml, economy/*.js). `ttl guild|merit|econ expect <bot>
# <field> <value>` print "ttl: ..." when the value is wrong, which `server.sh test-all` counts as a failure.
# Bot A is a Life 2 soul (test hook: stage ttl.life2); bot B stays in Life 1 and must be refused.
# Coin amounts are in bronze (1 silver = 10, 1 gold = 100). The bots keep their data between runs, so every record is
# reset first. Needs the reputation package (WP3: `ttl rep set|expect`) and, for the coin counts, Lightman's Currency
# or the inventory fallback (economy/sinks.js logs "[ttl] econ: ..." once when it falls back).
# Expect in the log: "[ttl] guild board <date>" after the roll, "[ttl] guild: TtlBotGuildA completed iron_order: 30 bronze",
# "... completed rabbit_cull: 20 bronze", and no "[ttl] economy command failed".
ttlbot spawn TtlBotGuildA
ttlbot spawn TtlBotGuildB
@sleep 2
ttl guild test TtlBotGuildA life2
ttl guild reset TtlBotGuildA
ttl merit reset TtlBotGuildA
ttl rep set TtlBotGuildA dwargon 0
clear TtlBotGuildA
execute in minecraft:overworld run tp TtlBotGuildA 100 100 100
# The board: 3 daily + 2 weekly, one daily slot for rank F; a Life 1 soul is refused (answers life2only, no side effects).
ttl guild roll
ttl guild expect TtlBotGuildA board 5
ttl guild expect TtlBotGuildB refuse_take life2only
ttl guild expect TtlBotGuildA rank F
ttl guild expect TtlBotGuildA stage none
# Deliver bounty: not ready until the 16 iron ingots are in the inventory; hand-in takes them and pays 3 silver.
ttl guild post iron_order
execute as TtlBotGuildA run ttl guild take iron_order
ttl guild expect TtlBotGuildA accepted_iron_order true
ttl guild expect TtlBotGuildA ready_iron_order false
give TtlBotGuildA minecraft:iron_ingot 16
ttl guild expect TtlBotGuildA ready_iron_order true
execute as TtlBotGuildA run ttl guild turnin
ttl guild expect TtlBotGuildA done 1
ttl guild expect TtlBotGuildA points 1
ttl guild expect TtlBotGuildA balance 30
ttl guild expect TtlBotGuildA stage F
ttl guild expect TtlBotGuildA ready_iron_order false
ttl rep expect TtlBotGuildA dwargon value 1
# Kill bounty: eight rabbit kills (faked on the objective), sampled, handed in for 2 silver. A bounty can be done once a day.
ttl guild post rabbit_cull
execute as TtlBotGuildA run ttl guild take rabbit_cull
scoreboard players add TtlBotGuildA ttl.g.tensura_horned_rabbit 8
ttl guild sample TtlBotGuildA
ttl guild expect TtlBotGuildA ready_rabbit_cull true
execute as TtlBotGuildA run ttl guild turnin
ttl guild expect TtlBotGuildA done 2
ttl guild expect TtlBotGuildA points 2
ttl guild expect TtlBotGuildA balance 50
# Sinks: a fee is charged from the carried coins and the change comes back; a poor player is refused.
ttl econ expect TtlBotGuildA fee_charter 5000
ttl econ expect TtlBotGuildA can_50 true
ttl econ expect TtlBotGuildA can_51 false
ttl econ take TtlBotGuildA 25
ttl econ expect TtlBotGuildA balance 25
ttl econ give TtlBotGuildA 5
ttl econ expect TtlBotGuildA balance 30
ttl econ
# Merit-lite: 100 merit in a marked Public Works chunk (cap 100 a week per chunk), then nothing more; the Builder title is
# 500 merit away. Other blocks and unmarked chunks earn nothing.
ttl merit test TtlBotGuildA stone_bricks 3
ttl merit expect TtlBotGuildA total 0
execute as TtlBotGuildA run ttl merit works mark
ttl merit expect TtlBotGuildA works 1
ttl merit test TtlBotGuildA dirt 5
ttl merit expect TtlBotGuildA total 0
ttl merit test TtlBotGuildA stone_bricks 100
ttl merit expect TtlBotGuildA total 100
ttl merit test TtlBotGuildA stone_bricks 5
ttl merit expect TtlBotGuildA total 100
ttl merit expect TtlBotGuildA builder false
execute as TtlBotGuildA run ttl merit works unmark
ttl merit expect TtlBotGuildA works 0
# Clean up.
ttl guild reset TtlBotGuildA
ttl merit reset TtlBotGuildA
clear TtlBotGuildA
ttlbot remove TtlBotGuildA
ttlbot remove TtlBotGuildB
